From 2e4058e792d71a979be66d89851ea9a2d9845d02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:01:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(app,motion): judge probe and plasma on a
 reduced-fidelity model; the cone and engrave rides stay refused for a stated
 reason

Probe's protected-move law (ball distance and stem/body solid law) and
plasma's kerf and cover laws give a coarse model's excess back out of
their slack while a positive slack is left (the #864 rule); past that
the program gate refuses the operation by name. Both kinds leave the
refused list in fidelity_law::excess_aware, and floor_of lists their
own slacks.

The cone and engrave rides stay refused: no tolerance holds the ride to
the model, so there is nothing to tighten (reason in fidelity_law's
header and docs/decisions/1053-fidelity-probe-plasma.md). The cross
drill stays refused: its standoff readings measure the mesh with no
slack; that remainder keeps #1053 open.

Refs #1053

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
