From c4648016563746cd2291d1c88ee29b530d6c8ef6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:06:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] test(plasma): drive the cover-law pin through
 plasma_profile

Re-review item on #1081: the pin called cover_law directly with the
tightened tolerance, so reverting cut()'s cover reach to plain KERF_TOL
stayed green. The pin now cuts a plate whose top edge carries a notch
narrower than the kerf; the offset bridges it, and the notch depth is
set from the bridged cut's own chords (geometry, not the law) so the
farthest floor point sits midway between the plain and the tightened
reach. plasma_profile cuts it at full fidelity and refuses it by name
at model_excess 0.007; reverting the call site to KERF_TOL fails it.

Refs #1053

